# The loop guard: is the goal already met, and is this check a repeat? (26 cases).
#
# This is the point with the largest measured waste behind it. In a preregistered study of
# 4,644 coding-agent runs, runs that fell into redundant verification at its extreme level
# cost 18x the clean-run median, made 2.5x the tool calls and took 3x the wall time, with no
# improvement in success (arXiv 2608.01347, Weinberger and Hozez, 2026).
#
# goal_met:      goal + what the agent has established -> true | false. The false cases are
#                the dangerous ones: a run that is nearly finished looks finished, and an
#                agent told to stop one step early loses the deliverable. Hard negatives
#                include a goal with two parts where only one is done, and a `done` that
#                records attempts rather than results.
# repeats_check: goal + done + the pending action -> true | false. Hard negatives: a check
#                that looks identical but runs after a change, and the same fact checked
#                against a different source, which is corroboration, not repetition.
#
# Both are binary, so AUC, Brier and ECE are computable. Single-annotator, authored
# 2026-09-24. Mixed Spanish and English content, because this point is harness-shaped
# rather than investigation-shaped.
